{"word": "glue", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "glue", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ɡluː/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ɡljuː/", "tags": ["obsolete"]}], "forms": [{"word": "glues", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "A hard gelatin made by boiling bones and hides, used in solution as an adhesive; or any sticky adhesive substance.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": ["Near-synonyms: adhesive, cement"], "quotes": [{"text": "The wasp has always made the paper from which it constructs its nest, by uniting vegetable fibres with glue, while man was vexing himself with attempts to write on the bark of trees or a waxen or metallic table.", "reference": "1832 July 25, “Review: Habits of Insects”, in North American Review, volume 35, number 76, →JSTOR, page 217:"}, {"text": "During the next few days, while the meat dried, they were both busy. They finished the bowl boat and coated it with the glue Jondalar made by boiling down the hooves, bone, and hide scraps.", "reference": "1990, Jean Marie Auel, chapter 9, in The Plains of Passage (Earth's Children), New York: Random House, published 2010, →ISBN, page 145:"}], "synonyms": ["adhesive", "cement"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "ab", "name": "Abkhaz"}, "word": "аҷаб"}, {"language": {"code": "af", "name": "Afrikaans"}, "word": "gom"}, {"language": {"code": "akl", "name": "Aklanon"}, "word": "pilit"}, {"language": {"code": "sq", "name": "Albanian"}, "word": "zamkë"}, {"language": {"code": "sq", "name": "Albanian"}, "word": "ngjitje"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "غِرَاء"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "لِزَاق"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "لِصَاق"}, {"language": {"code": "arz", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "لزاق"}, {"language": {"code": "arz", "name": "Arabic"}, "word":